  "prefLabel": "Psyc 102.05 Committees",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Psyc 102.05 Committees.\n\n(a) Pursuant to RSA 329-B: 4, and in accordance with its requirements, the board shall create and administer the following standing committees:\n\n(1) The advisory committee;\n\n(2) The committee for professional conduct investigations; and\n\n(3) The professional’s health committee.\n\n(b) The members of each standing committee shall meet the eligibility requirements set forth in RSA 329-B: 6.\n\n(c) Any other committee appointed by the board to make recommendations on matters within the statutory authority of the board, shall:\n\n(1) Be deemed a special committee to exist only until completion of its assigned task;\n\n(2) Consist of one or more members of the board; and\n\n(3) Be chaired by a member of the board.\n\n(d) Standing committees and special committees shall make recommendations to the board, but shall not take final action on behalf of the board.\n\nSource. #12035-A, eff 11-4-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/psyc100-500.html"
